== Architectural Limitation

The architecture's main limits are single points in the data tier (AISS-01, AISS-05, AISS-10), unproven capacity (AISS-12), drills not yet run on AWS (AISS-13) and unproven alarm delivery (AISS-16). @tbl-aiss separates recorded accepted exceptions from proposed production work. AISS-20 retains the deliberate shared-dev shift-left design and its artefact-reproducibility limit (§5.2), not an obligation to duplicate checks; AISS-21 and AISS-22 separately cover release-image rescanning and provenance.

*Roadmap.* Each open item is assigned to one phase (@tbl-roadmap). R0 is closed: the sessions of 9–11 November supplied the placement evidence (AISS-07), two rebuilds from zero and the load reruns (§4.1). The drills of AISS-13 and the fix of AISS-14 were not run by the status date and move to R1. R1 and R2 apply only if the platform continues after the course; their dates assume a go-live decision in December 2026.

